Requested by App::karr (its board, ticket #107). karr needs to answer one
question about a checkout: "is anything under this path tracked?", for a file
and a directory alike. That is prefix matching over the index, and through the
currently attached surface libgit2 cannot do it, so karr shells out to
`git ls-files -z` for what CLAUDE.md calls a local operation -- not as a
fallback from a native attempt, but because there is no native attempt to make.

Missing, and it is exactly one line:

    int git_index_find_prefix(size_t *at_pos, git_index *index, const char *prefix);

Attaches the same way as its exact-path sibling on line 389:

    _attach git_index_find_prefix  => [ 'size_t*', 'git_index', 'string' ] => 'int';

Everything else the caller needs is ALREADY attached -- verified against the
checkout, not assumed: git_repository_index (line 121), git_index_free (390),
git_index_find (389), git_index_get_byindex, git_index_entrycount. So this is
the single gap in an otherwise complete path.

Semantics worth pinning down in the POD and the test, because both are sharp:

- Returns 0 and writes the position on a hit, GIT_ENOTFOUND when no entry
  carries the prefix. at_pos may be NULL when the caller only wants the
  yes/no answer -- confirm Platypus passes a NULL through for 'size_t*' or
  document that a scalar ref is required.
- The match is a STRING prefix, not a path prefix. "tasks" also matches
  "tasksfoo.txt". A caller asking about a directory has to pass the trailing
  slash itself; a caller asking about a single file wants git_index_find
  instead. Say so where someone will read it.

Test alongside t/ coverage for git_index_find: an index with a nested entry,
one probe that hits via the directory prefix, one that misses, and one that
demonstrates the "tasks" / "tasksfoo.txt" trap so the semantics stay pinned.

Downstream consumer: Git::Native has no index API at all (Repository exposes
44 methods, none named index), so that repo gets its own ticket, which this
one blocks.
Binding, POD and test landed, uncommitted in the worktree (Changes deliberately untouched -- main agent writes that entry).

Signature verified against the installed header (/usr/include/git2/index.h:722, libgit2 1.5.1, Alien::Libgit2 install_type=system):
    GIT_EXTERN(int) git_index_find_prefix(size_t *at_pos, git_index *index, const char *prefix);
Attached as [ size_t*, git_index, string ] => int, next to git_index_find.

Empirical findings, all probed against 1.5.1 before being written down:
- undef for at_pos IS passed through as NULL. rc=0 on a hit, GIT_ENOTFOUND on a miss, no die. Documented as the supported yes/no form; a scalar ref is NOT mandatory.
- On a miss libgit2 does not touch the out-param, and Platypus copies the caller value back unchanged (preset 12345 survived). So an unset `my $pos` returns as 0 -- indistinguishable from a real hit at position 0. Pinned in POD and test: only trust the position when rc == 0.
- String prefix confirmed: with only tasksfoo.txt left, "tasks/" -> GIT_ENOTFOUND while "tasks" -> 0 at the position of tasksfoo.txt.

Test mutation-checked: retyping the out-param as opaque (the classic trap in the house rules) turns 3 of the new assertions red, so the coverage is not vacuous.

prove -lr t/ green: 26 files, 5226 tests.

Two pieces of adjacent drift found and filed instead of fixed here: #10 (the existing git_index_find test passes a raw pointer for size_t*, Platypus does not write through it, so its position assertion cannot fail) and #11 (git_index_find POD claims UINT_MAX on a miss; it returns GIT_ENOTFOUND).
